+              // stalls above the raw-body layer). Stream.timeoutOrElse is
+              // verified in effect 4.0.0-beta.83 with per-pull idle semantics
+              // ("The timeout is checked for each pull") — it resets on every
+              // parsed event, exactly the required behavior. Stream.timeoutFail
+              // does NOT exist in this version.
+              Stream.timeoutOrElse({
+                duration: Duration.millis(llmIdleTimeout),
+                orElse: () =>
+                  Stream.fail(
+                    new ProviderError.ResponseStreamError(
+                      `Turn stalled: no parsed stream event within ${llmIdleTimeout}ms`,
+                    ),
+                  ),
+              }),
               Stream.mapEffect((event) => LLMAISDK.toLLMEvents(state, event)),
               Stream.flatMap((events) => Stream.fromIterable(events)),
             )
```

The `ResponseStreamError` (code `ProviderResponseStreamError`) thrown here flows into the same bounded retry budget (Patch C) — the raw-body and parsed-stream deadlines are one coherent idle-progress policy across layers.

**Hunk D3 — instrumentation (kept from #180 §5.2.1, mandatory):** at stream start in the same composition, log response metadata (content-type, transport, provider/model/session) and emit a per-parsed-event DEBUG progress line (elapsed-since-last-parsed-event). The real-provider capture (test 15) then records the actual stall layer; the *next* hang is self-identifying.

