## 3. Non-SSE deadline and numeric chain (B2, V4 CLOSED)

### 3.1 Mechanism (unchanged from #180 — Option A')

`bodyIdleTimeout` (idle-progress, resets per chunk; slow-but-progressing bodies never aborted) for the non-SSE branch, distinct from `chunkTimeout` (SSE). Optional `bodyAbsoluteTimeout` belt-and-braces total cap, default OFF. Patch A/B implement it; the Option-B false-abort class analysis from #180 §3.4 is retained.

### 3.2 Numeric chain — re-derived against the PROJECT's 15–20 m operator-timeout ladder (V4 CLOSED)

The #180 chain compared a *chain total* (30 min) against a *per-request* bound (60 min request `timeout`) and then against an assumed 1 h operator timeout — the wrong ladder. SESSION-START §4a fixes task-matched operator-timeout ceilings: trivial ≤10 m, doc/simple/review **15–20 m**, port/multi-file 30 m, complex multi-phase 45 m+.

**Production values:**

| Knob | Value | Relation |
|---|---|---|
| `bodyIdleTimeout` | **300 000 ms (5 min)** — parity with production `chunkTimeout` | per-request idle < request `timeout` (5 min < 60 min) ✔ |
| `bodyAbsoluteTimeout` | 3 300 000 ms (55 min), **opt-in, default OFF** | < request `timeout` (55 min < 60 min) ✔ |
| `RETRY_MAX_RETRIES` | 2 (⇒ exactly 3 POSTs for the bounded class) | — |
| Worst case to terminal ERROR | `300 000 × 3` = **15 min** (+ ~6 s backoff) | **≤ 15 m floor** of the 15–20 m doc/review tier; **< 20 m** ceiling; **< 30 m / 45 m+** longer tiers |

**Invariant (the rule r1 asked for):**
`bodyIdleTimeout × (RETRY_MAX_RETRIES + 1) ≤ smallest operator timeout in use (15 m floor of the 15–20 m tier)` — 15 min ≤ 15 min. Equality at the floor is by design: it is exactly the SSE path's worst case (production `chunkTimeout=300000` ⇒ 15-min SSE detection), so non-SSE detection latency is **parity, not 2× slower** (the asymmetry r1 flagged). Strict `<` holds against the 20 m ceiling and every longer tier.

**Recorded exception — trivial ≤10 m tier:** for tasks launched at ≤10 m, the operator kill fires before the terminal ERROR surfaces (15 min > 10 min). Their protection is the outer net (operator timeout + #146 watcher restart) **plus** the per-attempt WARN lines emitted at ~5-min cadence — the failure is no longer silent (the pre-fix signature was an unbounded silent hang). This is the documented, accepted exception for the shortest tier; every task ≥ 15 m sees the ERROR before any outer kill.

**Per-attempt ceiling:** each POST is bounded by the first of {`bodyIdleTimeout` fire (5 min idle), `bodyAbsoluteTimeout` if set (55 min), request `timeout` (60 min)} — in every realistic hang the idle timer fires first.

**Alternative strict-form one-knob** (recorded, not primary): if strict `<` at the 15 m floor is ever demanded, `bodyIdleTimeout = 240 000` (4 min ⇒ 12 min < 15 min strictly) is the single change; cost is non-SSE detection 20% faster than SSE (asymmetry in the safe direction).

